            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "3.2.22 Using AR’s scaling feature, I adjusted this recipe from 120 servings to 6 servings. To say I ended up with some pretty wonky ingredient amounts is putting it mildly, and some of this recipe’s amounts just didn’t make sense to me even at 120 servings. I started off trying to stick with the ingredients listed, but this soup desperately needed seasoning. I used fresh green beans and carrots just because I had them in the fridge, and added part of a small zucchini I had left. I replaced some of the water with chicken broth (most, actually) and then when the soup needed more liquid, added the end of a carton of beef stock I had in the fridge. Your pasta will soak up the liquid, so keep an eye on that. Also, I added a bay leaf and some garlic powder, and basically, added more of the recipe ingredients until I reached a taste level that was satisfactory to me. I think this could be improved using beef broth instead of chicken and canned tomatoes instead of tomato sauce (or maybe “in addition to”), although I did use spicy El Pato tomato sauce (and more of it than listed) which really kicked up the flavor. This turned out OK, but doubtful I’ll make again. AR has a number of good “hamburger soups” on site, so I’ll probably just stick with them.",
            "datePublished": "2022-03-02T19:34:43.294Z"
          }
